<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The window background shown between process start and Compose's first frame.

  It can no longer be kept exactly in step with the scheme, and that is a real
  change: the theme is now chosen at runtime, so there are eight possible first
  frames (five presets, two modes) plus Material You and the pure-black option.
  A platform theme is resolved before any of that is read.

  So this APPROXIMATES the default preset, ThemeSeed.WADA, whose background is
  #F9F9F9 light and #111314 dark. A user on another preset sees at most one
  frame of the default's neutral before their own scheme paints over it. Both
  values are near-neutral greys in every preset, which is what makes the
  approximation cheap; a strongly tinted preset would show a flash.
-->
<resources>
    <color name="launch_background">#FFF9F9F9</color>
    <!-- The launcher icon's background layer, and it is load-bearing rather
         than decorative: the foreground is black ink whose white line-work was
         keyed to transparent, so this colour is what shows through the Fool's
         eyes and spirals. On a dark surface those holes would disappear and the
         mark would read as a blob, so it is parchment. Deliberately NOT
         night-qualified, and deliberately NOT tied to the theme: a launcher
         icon looks the same whichever mode the phone is in, and it must not
         change when the user picks a different palette inside the app. -->
    <color name="ic_launcher_background">#FFE2D3CF</color>
</resources>
